ed"]},"sid":["itu-9ead329e-331d-4056-9a41-7238df054a8a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Action Research Booklet","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747253","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper reports from an ongoing research project on meaningful adoption and use of Generative Artificial Intelligence within the Communication Department of a Danish Municipality. Given its capacity to generate images, information, and text, GenAI models are positioned as being potentially transformative to cognitive tasks in knowledge work, raising concerns about skill displacement and a loss of meaning in the profession. This paper presents a set of sociotechnical principles for the introduction and integration of novel technologies, such as GenAI, while retaining meaningfulness in work. These principles were crafted by combining work design theory and extensive empirical material gathered through Action Design Research, in close collaboration with employees from the department. Centering the need for a common understanding of expectations for GenAI, the principles also point to the importance of organizational support to enable autonomous experimentation and accountability, while emphasizing transparency surrounding the decision-making process for the use of GenAI.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Marttila, Sanna-Maria","Sandbukt, Sunniva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759406"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","title":"European Conference on Information Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action Design Research","Generative AI","Sociotechnical Principles","Work design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crafting meaningful generative ai enabled knowledge work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106309094/Crafting_Meaningful_Generative_AI-Enabled_Knowledge_Work.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759406","ids":["itu-6aac332a-122b-4b49-a315-91b5cb88a459"],"keyword":["Action Design Research","Generative AI","Sociotechnical Principles","Work design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-567D1CDC6155A62357BE8A87B85C5BF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106309094/Crafting_Meaningful_Generative_AI-Enabled_Knowledge_Work.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sunniva","key":"sandbuktpau","last":"Sandbukt","locid":"06d038a4-f659-4c53-8a6d-58e295ab603f","name":"Sandbukt, Sunniva","orcid":"0009-0002-4274-4991","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"issue":"2024","journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","paperid":"10","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6aac332a-122b-4b49-a315-91b5cb88a459"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crafting Meaningful Generative AI-Enabled Knowledge Work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759406","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Du er på vej ind i et online-møde med vigtige samarbejdspartnere. I samme sekund popper meldingen op: En teknologi skal opdateres. Du må genstarte, gennemgå 10-12 trin, finde koder frem – og fem minutter for sent toner du frem på mødedeltagernes skærme med, hvad der opfattes som klodens dårligste undskyldning. Den om it-problemer. Du oplever et kontroltab, der kan føles uretfærdigt. De konstante notifikationer, nye features og viften af forskellige it-systemer på arbejdspladsen kan give digital stress. Men det er muligt at lære at navigere i det digitaliserede arbejdsmiljø med større indsigt. Forfatterne, Raluca A. Stana og Hanne Westh Nicolajsen, har solid forskningsbaseret ekspertise inden for digital transformation, organisation, arbejdsmiljø og technostress. Med Digital stress på arbejdspladsen har de skabt en håndbog for ledere og medarbejdere, som kortlægger sammenhængen mellem digitalisering og stress. Forfatterne præsenterer praktiske, strategiske værktøjer til at forebygge overbelastning af den enkelte og fremme en organisationskultur, der er med til at reducere digital stress.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Stana, Raluca Alexandra","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S02-097.14-785372"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Technostress"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital stress på arbejdspladsen en håndbog for ledere og medarbejdere","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://djoefforlag.dk/products/digital-stress-pa-arbejdspladsen","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.14-785372","ids":["itu-ceb23161-c947-4ef0-bde1-0d4c007ea926","ruc-a381ba22-d468-4489-8188-c3615004e480"],"keyword":["digital stress","technostress"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-1BDEBCD38D315803D3F8A54F6050DF73"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Raluca Alexandra","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","locid":"8e397dc6-de47-4c8b-b13d-7785d1d95d5f","name":"Stana, Raluca Alexandra","orcid":"0000-0002-2155-8295","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788757458961"],"isbn":["9788757458954"],"pages":"180","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ceb23161-c947-4ef0-bde1-0d4c007ea926","ruc-a381ba22-d468-4489-8188-c3615004e480"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Digital Stress på arbejdspladsen : En håndbog for ledere og medarbejdere","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.14-785372","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Technostress is a concern for research and practice. Existing Information Systems (IS) research on technostress tends to predominantly focus on the five technostress-creating dimensions (e.g., overload or invasion) identified two decades ago. However, the dynamic nature of IS and the technological and disciplinary advancements call for a re-examination of constructs. This study adopts a sociological lens, exploring obligations associated with Information and Communication Technologies (ICTs) use at work and their interrelationship to employees’ technostress experiences. We apply the concept of obligation to unpack technostress. Using interpretative research based on qualitative interviews, we identify several overlapping obligations that intensify technostress, such as the need to maintain productivity, manage ICT systems, and continuously learn to use new tools. While there is a social element in the creation of obligations, employees engage in these through habits. This study hints at several important aspects: (1) greater awareness of obligations and obligation-driven habits is needed for individuals and organizations to manage technostress; (2) organizations need to recognize the dual nature of ICTs as both enablers and barriers of productivity; (3) employees believe it is their individual obligation to manage technostress, but organizations need to also take responsibility in order to deal with technostress effectively.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Stana, Raluca Alexandra","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-801551"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digitalization","ICTs","Obligation","Organizations","Technostress"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from duty to distress a sociological exploration of technostress in organizations through the lens of obligations","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/108883944/From_duty_to_distress.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-801551","identifier":[{"id":"85214896471","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-ff7e4249-e5e7-43c0-95af-500ad8817563"],"keyword":["ICTs","Obligation","digitalization","organizations","technostress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2071B2961F898071F7195CB6B5EA7E8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/108883944/From_duty_to_distress.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/sjis/vol36/iss2/7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Sustainable Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Raluca Alexandra","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","locid":"8e397dc6-de47-4c8b-b13d-7785d1d95d5f","name":"Stana, Raluca Alexandra","orcid":"0000-0002-2155-8295","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09050167"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","paperid":"7","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Information Systems","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214896471"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-ff7e4249-e5e7-43c0-95af-500ad8817563"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"From duty to distress. : A sociological exploration of technostress in organizations through the lens of obligations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-801551","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We investigate three small employee-owned businesses: a consultancy, a business within art restoration, and a software business, and how they apply and reshape digital resources to commonly govern their businesses as there is no single tool that caters to their specific needs. Using the concept of digital bricolage as a lens, we find that the businesses apply a combination of digital resources at hand to meet their needs, they use these tools in well-known ways, and create new solutions, but do not look for ideal solutions. We furthermore find that believing in a common set of values shapes “the bricolage”, an aspect not found in the literature. These shared values further inform how technologies are used in practice. The values are shared internally but differ between the businesses. This has implications for the design of future tools that can help businesses govern collective decision-making.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776381"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design","Employee ownership"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing it for governance the case of employee owned businesses the case of employee owned businesses","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776381","identifier":[{"id":"85200656394","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2680c5af-21f5-4d28-a533-141becbc0080"],"keyword":["Design","Digital bricolage","Employee ownership"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17D899CE01A