{"abstract":"The cooperative model is known for its resilience and objective that prioritizes the common needs of their members, rather than returns for shareholders. The governance model follows a value-driven logic and a democratic structure, in that decision making is based on the “one person - one vote” principle. Under this umbrella, employee-owned businesses (EOBs) are organizations where the employees own and manage the company. Like other types of cooperatives, they arevalue driven, member owned, and democratically controlled organizations; principles that explain why EOBs have been economically sound and more resilient to crisis, such as Covid, compared to other types of organizations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Baka, Vasiliki","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718937"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cooperative","Cooperative governance","Digital era","employee owned businesses"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enacting cooperative governance in the digital era","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718937","ids":["itu-fd496beb-db0f-4958-93f1-7e992332a335"],"keyword":["Cooperative","cooperative governance","digital era","employee-owned businesses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D4A7CC146CC675D0349F2C2DE0EE63D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fd496beb-db0f-4958-93f1-7e992332a335"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enacting cooperative governance in the digital era","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718937","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Velkommen til antologien “Studier af relevante og tidstypiske digitale udfordringer i en dansk/nordisk kontekst.” Antologien er rettet til ledere og ansvarlige for digitaliseringsaktiviteter i danske virksomheder og organisationer, som er nysgerrige på den forskning, der foregår på IT-universitetets institut ”Business IT”. Vi har samlet en række artikler som viser et bredt udsnit af den forskning som foregår på instituttet Business IT - i daglig tale kaldet BIT. BIT har et større antal forskere, der til dagligt forsker og underviser i de mange aspekter og bevægelser, som digitalisering afføder i samfundet og i offentlige som private virksomheder. Oftest er vores artikler på engelsk. Mange af forskerne er internationale og kommer fra forskellige regioner i verdenen. Sammen deltager vi på konferencer i udlandet og udgiver i engelsksprogede tidsskrifter. Med denne udgivelse har vi valgt at gøre noget ved den engelsksprogede formidlingstradition, idet vi som et eksperiment har fået oversat otte artikler til dansk af bureauet Hurtigoversætter. Vi mener de otte artikler er relevante og aktuelle i en dansk kontekst, og så dækker de bredt over hvad BIT-forskerne interesserer sig for og forsker i. Studierne spænder bredt i både deres tilgang inden for forskningsområderne: Informationssystemer (IS), Computer Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW) og Science and Technology Studies (STS). Ligeledes er der anvendt forskellige dataindsamlingsmetoder såsom etnografiske studier, casestudier og kvantitative undersøgelser. I samlingen finder du således studier om anvendelse af digitalisering på samfundsplan samt på organisationsplan i såvel private som offentlige virksomheder. Nogle studier har fokus på implementering af bestemte platformsteknologier eller teknologier som blockchain, AI eller fænomener som e-valg. Andre handler om ledelsesopgaven i relation til digitaliseringsstrategier og innovation, ledelse af medarbejdere under Covid-19 eller udfordringer med teknostress i forbindelse med den stigende digitalisering.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383872"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Computer Supported Cooperative Work CSCW","Digitalization","Information systems IS","Science and Technology Studies STS"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"studier af relevante og tidstypiske digital udfordringer i en dansk nordisk kontekst en forskningsantologi fra business it instituttet på it universitetet i københavn","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383872","ids":["itu-b2bc6242-2556-4729-8434-850b991b86a9"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Computer Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW)","Digitalization","Information Systems (IS)","Science and Technology Studies (STS)"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4E800E0E58E547BC3A4DC6809B201F36"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerped","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenped","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788779496484"],"pages":"139","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b2bc6242-2556-4729-8434-850b991b86a9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Studier af relevante og tidstypiske digital udfordringer i en dansk/nordisk kontekst : en forskningsantologi fra Business IT-instituttet på IT-Universitetet i København","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383872","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"I meget digitaliserede lande som Danmark, viser statistikken, at en ud af fire ansatte har oplevet højestressniveauer. Dog er viden om dette fænomen, på trods af omfattende forskningsbeviser for tilstedeværelsen af technostress, endnu ikke en del af materialet og vejledningerne fra officielle myndigheder. Tidligere forskning i technostress har givet kvantitative psykologiske og neurofysiologiske perspektiver på technostress med fokus på individet, teknologien eller det teknologiske miljø. Vi betragter dette som en begrænset tilgang, da den udelukker det sociale miljø, hvor technostress opstår. Vores hensigt er at vise de sociologiske mekanismer, som bidrager til technostress ved at bruge en sociologisk pligtlinse. Vi spørger: 'Hvilken viden kan den sociologiske pligtlinse tilføre den teoretiske forståelse af technostress?' Til at besvare vores forskningsspørgsmål bruger vi et indlejret casestudie i Danmark ved at se på det eksisterende politiske materiale og interviews med 14 ansatte fra seks forskellige organisationer. Vi mener, at stress i praksis mest betragtes fra et responsperspektiv, som peger på individet. Denne synsvinkel er en iboende del af, hvordan individer tager ansvar for den technostress, de oplever. Et andet kritisk resultat fra vores data er, at technostress er socialt konstrueret. Vores teoretiske bidrag er anvendelsen af en for IS ukendt teori, og en kvalitativ tilgang til forskning i technostress, som giver os mulighed for at afdække, hvordan den sociale pligtkonstruktion påvirker den enkelte ansatte. Vores teoretiske bidrag peger på behovet for en praksis, som bevæger sig i retning af at betragte technostress som et samfundsmæssigt snarere end et udelukkende individuelt ansvar.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stana, Raluca","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381703"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["teknostress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sociologiske mekanismer bag ikt relateret technostress på arbejdspladsen","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381703","ids":["itu-1d258262-d15e-49b8-9ca9-921bbd99916f"],"keyword":["teknostress"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6042A829832BFC5D8B5288AF072B201F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raluca","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","name":"Stana, Raluca","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"harderfischerpedh","last":"Harder Fischer","name":"Harder Fischer, Louise","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpedh","last":"Nicolajsen","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9788779496484"],"pages":"41-61","place":"ITU","status":"p","subtitle":"En forskningsantologi fra Business IT-instituttet på IT-Universitetet i København","title":"Studier af relevante og tidstypiske digitale udfordringer i en dansk/nordisk kontekst"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1d258262-d15e-49b8-9ca9-921bbd99916f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SOCIOLOGISKE MEKANISMER BAG IKT-RELATERET TECHNOSTRESS PÅ ARBEJDSPLADSEN","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381703","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Digitalization is followed by technological opportunities as well as consequences such as technostress. Information Systems (IS) technostress research is built upon stress research assumptions, which are deeply rooted in positivist ontologies. In this paper, we take a social constructivist perspective, and we ask the question: How is technostress made in the workplace? We answer this question by employing a case study from Denmark across multiple Danish private organizations. We find that individuals work under deeply rooted and outdated obligations, some dating from the industrialization age (e.g., working from nine to five). Moreover, life in a highly digitalized society places additional pressure leading to technostress, as employees are also citizens. We invite IS research to consider how we might contribute as a discipline to an increasingly digitalization agenda, one that recognizes the unique position we find ourselves in as a discipline through uniting both the dystopian and utopian perspectives on digitalization and finding balance.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Stana, Raluca Alexandra","Nicolaisen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S02-083.33-038295"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","end":"2022-08-17","place":"Helsinge, dk","start":"2022-08-14","title":"45th Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Digitalization","Obligations","Technostress","Technostress Digitalization Obligations"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"if digitalization is the answer then what was the question a case study of how technostress is made","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101333666/If_Digitalization_is_the_Answer_Then_What_Was_the_Question_A_Case_Study_of_How_Technostress_is_Made.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.33-038295","ids":["itu-46dbbfdf-da4b-488a-a9ba-e09ab91c69d8","ruc-c1d4fb37-8f2f-4573-9d9a-8408338f0644"],"keyword":["Digitalization","Obligations","Technostress","Technostress, Digitalization, Obligations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-FF173577706BA123C4A019175A897242"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1006&context=iris2022","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/iris2022/7/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101333666/If_Digitalization_is_the_Answer_Then_What_Was_the_Question_A_Case_Study_of_How_Technostress_is_Made.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Raluca Alexandra","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","locid":"8e397dc6-de47-4c8b-b13d-7785d1d95d5f","name":"Stana, Raluca Alexandra","orcid":"0000-0002-2155-8295","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863","23873353"],"issn_org":["18919863"],"issue":"1","journal":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","paperid":"7","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","status":"p","title":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-46dbbfdf-da4b-488a-a9ba-e09ab91c69d8","ruc-c1d4fb37-8f2f-4573-9d9a-8408338f0644"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"If Digitalization is the Answer, Then What Was the Question? : A Case Study of How Technostress is Made","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.33-038295","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Udbredelsen og kendskabet til demokratiske virksomheder er begrænset både i det danske samfund, i undervisningssystemet og ikke mindst i rådgivningssystemet. De demokratiske virksomheder kan noget andet end de mere traditionelle virksomheder foruden, at de kan styrke iværksætteri. Det er derfor et problem, at rådgivning og uddannelse i demokratisk iværksætteri er fraværende eller begrænset. Der er således et stort potentiale i at fremme demokratiske virksomhedsformer og demokratisk iværksætteri, men opgaven i at styrke forståelsen og rådgivningen af demokratiske virksomheder er betragtelig. Hvis demokratisk iværksætteri skal tages alvorligt og blive en vigtig spiller samfundsmæssigt, som det er i andre EU-lande, skal det have større politisk bevågenhed og satsning, herunder introduceres i undervisningssystemet.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Victor, Fie Foged","Sivertsen, Stine","Baka, Vasiliki","Stana, Raluca Alexandra","Hansen, Anne Vorre","Riisgaard, Lone","Jakobsen, Gurli"],"cuid":["S02-097.13-038418"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"demokratisk iværksætteri erhvervsfremme og iværksætteri for demokratiske virksomheder i danmark sammenfatning","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/85229673/Demokratisk_Iv_rks_tteri.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.13-038418","ids":["itu-fd55a44d-95c3-4819-bf45-fc7d8cafa6ec","ruc-093741bc-4d76-47bd-98be-f01b3b26fea0"],"keyword":["Democratic Entrepreneurship"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","