ctor, Fie Foged","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-096f16ae-7e3f-4368-9ce7-0438d9d05e94"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Employee-owned startups in the digital era","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381395","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In patients with atopic dermatitis (AD), Staphylococcus aureus frequently colonizes lesions and is hypothesized to be linked to disease severity and progression. Treatments that reduce S. aureus colonization without significantly affecting the skin commensal microbiota are needed. METHODS AND FINDINGS: In this study, we tested ATx201 (niclosamide), a small molecule, on its efficacy to reduce S. aureus and propensity to evolve resistance in vitro. Various cutaneous formulations were then tested in a superficial skin infection model. Finally, a Phase 2 randomized, double-blind and placebo-controlled trial was performed to investigate the impact of ATx201 OINTMENT 2% on S. aureus colonization and skin microbiome composition in patients with mild-to-severe AD (EudraCT:2016-003501-33). ATx201 has a narrow minimal inhibitory concentration distribution (.125-.5 μg/ml) consistent with its mode of action - targeting the proton motive force effectively stopping cell growth. In murine models, ATx201 can effectively treat superficial skin infections of methicillin-resistant S. aureus. In a Phase 2 trial in patients with mild-to-severe AD (N = 36), twice-daily treatment with ATx201 OINTMENT 2% effectively reduces S. aureus colonization in quantitative colony forming unit (CFU) analysis (primary endpoint: 94.4% active vs. 38.9% vehicle success rate, p = .0016) and increases the Shannon diversity of the skin microbiome at day 7 significantly compared to vehicle. CONCLUSION: These results suggest that ATx201 could become a new treatment modality as a decolonizing agent.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Weiss, Anne","Delavenne, Emilie","Matias, Carina","Lagler, Heimo","Simon, Daniel","Li, Ping","Hansen, Jon U","Pires dos Santos, Teresa M S","Jana, Bimal","Priemel, Petra A.","Bangert, Christine","Bauer, Martin","Eberl, Sabine","Nussbaumer-Pröll, Alina","Anne Österreicher, Zoe","Matzneller, Peter","Quint, Tamara","Weber, Maria","Nielsen, Hanne Mørck","Rades, Thomas","Johansen, Helle Krogh","Westh, Henrik","Kim, Wooseong","Mylonakis, Eleftherios","Friis, Christian","Guardabassi, Luca","Pace, John","Lundberg, Carina Vingsbo","M'Zali, Fatima","Butty, Pascal","Sørensen, Nikolaj","Nielsen, Henrik Bjørn","Toft-Kehler, Rasmus","Guttman-Yassky, Emma","Stingl, Georg","Zeitlinger, Markus","Sommer, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-498355"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brown University","Ceva Santé Animale","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Medical University of Vienna","Université de Bordeaux"],"keyword":["Animals","Anti Bacterial Agents pharmacology","Dermatitis Atopic drug therapy","Humans","Methicillin Resistant Staphylococcus aureus","Mice","Microbiota","Staphylococcal Infections drug therapy","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"topical niclosamide atx000000000201 reduces i staphylococcus aureus i colonization and increases shannon diversity of the skin microbiome in atopic dermatitis patients in a randomized double blind placebo controlled phase 000000000002 trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ctm2.790","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-498355","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9076020","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35522900","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-afa75a43-2936-4cd1-a8ed-899282e9fedc"],"keyword":["Animals","Anti-Bacterial Agents/pharmacology","Dermatitis, Atopic/drug therapy","Humans","Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus aureus","Mice","Microbiota","Niclosamide/pharmacology","Ointments/pharmacology","Staphylococcal Infections/drug therapy","Staphylococcus aureus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E08858F95DDFE842AD91C42C146AF617"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/322672167/1_s2.0_S0160412022004718_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ctm2.790","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["UNION Therapeutics"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"medical university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical University of Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University o