{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Tjørnehøj, Gitte","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382556"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"successful innovation in tele care continuous co creation and situated re innovation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.amazon.com/Beyond-Interpretivism-Encounters-Technology-Organization-ebook/dp/B01MSNVCTJ","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382556","ids":["itu-570bdcd7-a04a-4bf0-acfe-eea79bec6d3a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7F9302283BEED85621D6CCD4AB1F17C1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"tjørnehøjpau","last":"Tjørnehøj","name":"Tjørnehøj, Gitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"westhnicolajsenpau","last":"Westh Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","name_org":"Westh Nicolajsen, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783319497327"],"publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Beyond Interpretivism? New Encounters with Technology and Organization"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-570bdcd7-a04a-4bf0-acfe-eea79bec6d3a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Successful Innovation in Tele-Care : Continuous Co-creation and Situated Re-Innovation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382556","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"IT has become a vital part of our daily lives, requiring new skills among today’s leaders, who need to keep up with competitors and meet the needs of employees and customers. This applies to nearly every industry - from clothing manufacturers to logistics companies. However, many leaders find it difficult to keep up with the impacts of digitalization, but the ability to think and act in a digitally innovative way, is absolutely essential for business leaders. For example, most leaders need to be capable of exploiting the potential of collaborating virtually with employees, customers and business partners. If companies are not aware of “new digital opportunities” they will fail to provide their employees with the appropriate digital tools that support their daily tasks. For instance, we see the increase of ‘Shadow IT’: Employees use IT that is not officially approved by the company and that they own privately. This does not happen because the employees want to do something “illegal”, but simply because they feel it is necessary to use a more efficient tool (such as Whatsapp or Dropbox) to execute their tasks. This may have negative consequences for the companies. However, leaders who know how to leverage the use of shadow IT and think innovatively can gain a lot for their company. From September 2017 until January 2019, we tried to inspire the leaders and provide them with an overview of specific methods and tools to exploit digitalization, whilst reducing the risks associated with it.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Richter, Alexander","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Nielsen, Lene","Müller, Oliver","Krancher, Oliver","Stana, Raluca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383928"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Leadership"],"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"innovation for leadership","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85351311/I4L_Report.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383928","ids":["itu-b6646876-8803-4d5d-a538-294407a94d90"],"keyword":["Leadership"],"lang":"English","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6108B67CDCD71D9F7DD9974CC92B81BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85351311/I4L_Report.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","name":"Richter, Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, Oliver","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"krancherpau","last":"Krancher","locid":"f14f4742-c9d8-4a34-b8e2-d713c3a1f437","name":"Krancher, Oliver","orcid":"0000-0003-3876-3604","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raluca","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","name":"Stana, Raluca","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"26","publisher":"IT-Universitetet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b6646876-8803-4d5d-a538-294407a94d90"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Innovation for Leadership","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383928","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Digitalization in the public sector is growing to also include areas such as social care. We investigate the digital service innovation process within home care services in a Danish municipality. Inspired by theory on social materiality, we argue for an approach to digital service innovation within social care as an ongoing and entangled development of human and technological resources. We take an abductive approach as we combine theory on social-materiality and digital service innovation with empirical insights. Based in this, we propose five principles of importance for successful digital service innovation in social care: 1) mutual adaption; 2) piloting; 3) empowered; 4) situated re-innovation, and 5) continuous innovation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Tjørnehøj, Gitte","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382632"],"event":{"acronym":"HICSS","end":"2018-01-06","place":"Waikokoa Vilage, us","start":"2018-01-03","title":"Hawaii International Conference on Information Sciences 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital service innovation","Digitalization","Home Care Services","Social care","Social materiality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"five principles for digital service innovation in social care","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24251/HICSS.2018.136","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382632","identifier":[{"id":"85108289952","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5b8fe428-a67b-4872-9767-b39f7927290b"],"keyword":["Digital service innovation","Digitalization","Home care services","Social care","Social materiality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DCB36ED79C00C52758136F5DF17ED5CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/hicss-51/da/ict_enabled_services/8/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84375741/Five_Principles_for_Digital_Service_Innovation_in_Social_Care.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"http://hdl.handle.net/10125/50023","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24251/HICSS.2018.136","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"tjørnehøjpau","last":"Tjørnehøj","name":"Tjørnehøj, Gitte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.24251/hicss.2018.136","eisbn":["9780998133119"],"pages":"1086-1095","publisher":"AIS Electronic Library (AISeL)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 51st Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108289952"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5b8fe428-a67b-4872-9767-b39f7927290b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Five Principles for Digital Service Innovation in Social Care","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382632","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The digital transformation of the workplace impacts all involved individuals, including leaders, who have to balance institutionally implemented traditional organizational structures and new ways of working, enabled by digital platforms and (often) needed by their employees. Studies show that many leaders are still struggling to find their new individual leadership role and interaction style in the openness of the digital work environment. With this study, we want to contribute to a better understanding of actual digital leadership practices, i.e. how the digitization of the workplace changes leadership styles and approaches. Based on the theoretical lens of social intelligence, we identify five interwoven categories of digital leadership practices through a rigorous literature review and empirically refine them through a focus group as well as an illustrative case study: communicating, adapting, listening, understanding, and empathizing. Framing digital leadership through the lens of social intelligence allows us to emphasize the human perspective of this reconfiguration, which goes beyond ‘rewiring’ the work environment and acknowledges the fact that digital leaders need to learn socially intelligent behaviors.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stana, Raluca","Richter, Alexander","Trier, Matthias","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384799"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Information systems","Leadership"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital leadership practices a social intelligence perspective","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85351371/DIGITAL_LEADERSHIP_PRACTICES_A_SOCIAL_INTELLIGENCE_PERSPECTIVE_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384799","ids":["itu-efe3cf39-86e1-4d0b-9d76-aec7f1776305"],"keyword":["Information Systems","Leadership"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FB704C76021BA4366A18F7934BEDF00E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85351371/DIGITAL_LEADERSHIP_PRACTICES_A_SOCIAL_INTELLIGENCE_PERSPECTIVE_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raluca","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","name":"Stana, Raluca","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","name":"Richter, Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"trierpau","last":"Trier","name":"Trier, Matthias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"15","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-efe3cf39-86e1-4d0b-9d76-aec7f1776305"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital leadership practices: a social intelligence perspective","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384799","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This article presents the results of a study investigating user involvement in the idea generation phase of service innovation, and discusses advantages and limitations of such involvement. Specifically, the study compares the use of social media such as blogs and future workshops to generate idea for service innovations in the context of a research library. Our study shows that the blog is good in opening up for user contributions, while the future workshop involving users and employees is particularly good at qualifying and further developing ideas. The findings suggest therefore that methods for user involvement should be carefully selected and combined to achieve optimum benefits and avoid potential disadvantages","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nicolaisen, Hanne Westh","Sørensen, Flemming","Scupola, Ada"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-562336"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"user involvement in service innovation processes","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-562336","identifier":[{"id":"85065777384","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-5f8bc263-9735-4731-9f2b-4264fb232069"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-EA2492A34A2AF5EF53A7D6E5780BD68D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","