pau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"tjørnehøjpau","last":"Tjørnehøj","name":"Tjørnehøj, Gitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5f1c8b01-e21f-49e3-a37f-2097a5ce13b6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digitalizing Labor Intensive Services","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382702","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Small colony variants (SCVs) of the human pathogen Staphylococcus aureus are associated with persistent infections. Phenotypically, SCVs are characterized by slow growth and they can arise upon interruption of the electron transport chain that consequently reduce membrane potential and thereby limit uptake of aminoglycosides (e.g., gentamicin). In this study, we have examined the pathways by which the fitness cost of SCVs can be ameliorated. Five gentamicin resistant SCVs derived from S. aureus JE2 were independently selected on agar plates supplemented with gentamicin. The SCVs carried mutations in the menaquinone and hemin biosynthesis pathways, which caused a significant reduction in exponential growth rates relative to wild type (WT; 0.59-0.72) and reduced membrane potentials. Fifty independent lineages of the low-fitness, resistant mutants were serially passaged for up to 500 generations with or without sub-lethal concentrations of gentamicin. Amelioration of the fitness cost followed three evolutionary trajectories and was dependent on the initial mutation type (point mutation vs. deletion) and the passage condition (absence or presence of gentamicin). For SCVs evolved in the absence of gentamicin, 12 out of 15 lineages derived from SCVs with point mutations acquired intra-codonic suppressor mutations restoring membrane potential, growth rate, gentamicin susceptibility and colony size to WT levels. For the SCVs carrying deletions, all lineages enhanced fitness independent of membrane potential restoration without alterations in gentamicin resistance levels. By whole genome sequencing, we identified compensatory mutations in genes related to the σ(B) stress response (7 out of 10 lineages). Inactivation of rpoF that encode for the alternative sigma factor SigB (σ(B)) partially restored fitness of SCVs. For all lineages passaged in the presence of gentamicin, fitness compensation via membrane potential restoration was suppressed, however, selected for secondary mutations in fusA and SAUSA300_0749. This study is the first to describe fitness compensatory events in SCVs with deletion mutations and adaptation of SCVs to continued exposure to gentamicin.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Vestergaard, Martin","Paulander, Wilhelm Erik Axel","Leng, Bingfeng","Nielsen, Jesper B.","Westh, Henrik","Ingmer, Hanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-464230"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel pathways for ameliorating the fitness cost of gentamicin resistant small colony variants","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2016.01866","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-464230","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5119051","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27920765","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85006757688","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7655d7df-5d33-42c0-a684-25b9a0798067"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-232361DF25A56DD682C8AE0936C86A17"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/169940596/fmicb_07_01866_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2016.01866","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Food Safety and Zoonoses"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"0d6ed4a6-2995-46f9-9402-9e1ce154e032","name":"Vestergaard, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-3840-3193","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wilhelm Erik Axel","key":"paulanderpau","last":"Paulander","locid":"6a578093-fc01-4db3-9e17-074518c62644","name":"Paulander, Wilhelm Erik Axel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bingfeng","key":"lengpau","last":"Leng","locid":"b61cf8ae-b051-4a41-a71b-0a85e050a6e1","name":"Leng, Bingfeng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik T.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, Henrik T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27920765"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2016.01866","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"1866","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006757688"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7655d7df-5d33-42c0-a684-25b9a0798067"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Novel pathways for ameliorating the fitness cost of gentamicin resistant small colony variants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-464230","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Successful IT-enabled innovation is often attributed to benefit realization. However, often the results of the innovations are disappointing. Reason for this is argued to be a divide between development of the technological solution, and the organizational implementation and change that should ensure realization of the planned benefits. To handle this dilemma, it is advised to strengthen the management of the realization project accepting technology development and organizational change as entangled. Information technology is thus best described as a socio-material construct having the technical and the social inextricable linked. This paper challenges the belief in an inherent divide by suggesting integration of the technological and organizational development in the pilot-phase as well as subsequent phases through co-creation and situated re-innovation. With reference to a case on telecare this paper elaborates on co-creation and situated re-innovation and illustrates how this can be organized in practice.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Tjørnehøj, Gitte","Lundin, Johan","Lundh Snis, Ulrika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381639"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","end":"2016-08-10","place":"Ljungskile, se","start":"2016-08-07","title":"Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University West","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Situated Re Innovation Co creation Socio Materiality Benefits Realization Tele Care Public Sector Digitalization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"successful innovation in tele care continuous cocreation and situated re innovation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81635605/co_creation_re_innovation_IRIS2016.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381639","ids":["itu-18ff2fe5-436a-4ce3-9d13-edf9e93534ee"],"keyword":["Situated Re-Innovation, Co-creation, Socio-Materiality, Benefits Realization, Tele-Care, Public Sector, Digitalization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-392B0C9CBC24F4C475DE6747B9D38701"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81635605/co_creation_re_innovation_IRIS2016.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"university west","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University West","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"tjørnehøjpau","last":"Tjørnehøj","name":"Tjørnehøj, Gitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johan","key":"lundinped","last":"Lundin","name":"Lundin, Johan","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrika","key":"lundhsnisped","last":"Lundh Snis","name":"Lundh Snis, Ulrika","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"","first":"Johan","key":"lundinpedh","last":"Lundin","name":"Lundin, Johan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrika","key":"lundhsnispedh","last":"Lundh Snis","name":"Lundh Snis, Ulrika","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789187531385"],"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 39th Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia (IRIS 39) - Ljungskile, Sverige"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-18ff2fe5-436a-4ce3-9d13-edf9e93534ee"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Successful Innovation in Tele-Care: Continuous Cocreation and Situated Re-Innovation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381639","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Successful IT-enabled innovation is often attributed to benefit realization. However, often the results of the innovations are disappointing.Reason for this is argued to be a divide between development of the technological solution, and the organizational implementation and change thatshould ensure realization of the planned benefits. To handle this dilemma, it isadvised to strengthen the management of the realization project acceptingtechnology development and organizational change as entangled. Informationtechnology is thus best described as a socio-material construct having thetechnical and the social inextricable linked. This paper challenges the belief inan inherent divide by suggesting integration of the technological andorganizational development in the pilot-phase as well as subsequent phasesthrough co-creation and situated re-innovation. With reference to a case on telecare this paper elaborates on co-creation and situated re-innovation andillustrates how this can be organized in practice. AB - Successful IT-enabled innovation is often attributed to benefit realization. However, often the results of the innovations are disappointing.Reason for this is argued to be a divide between development of the technological solution, and the organizational implementation and change thatshould ensure realization of the planned benefits. To handle this dilemma, it isadvised to strengthen the management of the realization project acceptingtechnology development and organizational change as entangled. Informationtechnology is thus best described as a socio-material construct having thetechnical and the social inextricable linked. This paper challenges the belief inan inherent divide by suggesting integration of the technological andorganizational development in the pilot-phase as well as subsequent phasesthrough co-creation and situated re-innovation. With reference to a case on telecare this paper elaborates on co-creation and situated re-innovation andillustrates how this can be organized in practice.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Tjørnehøj, Gitte","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-114655"],"event":{"end":"2016-08-10","place":"Ljungskile, se","start":"2016-08-07","title":"The 39th Information Systems Research Conference in Scandinavia","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"successful innovation in tele care continuous cocreation and situated re innovation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-114655","ids":["aau-de26b8a2-161f-47fc-8775-65b80036fd01"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E0AC56D78DD5687F439F062CA80CE238"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, Centre for Information Systems Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Birgitte Bay","key":"tjørnehøjpau","last":"Tjørnehøj","locid":"0c313b43-1daa-4d6a-8b70-463c557e4b82","name":"Tjørnehøj, Gitte","name_org":"Tjørnehøj, Anne Birgitte Bay","orcid":"0000-0002-3630-5688","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"fc0c09b9-7317-48b6-9bdb-a