{"abstract":"In recent years there has been a growing interest in adopting social media to support students’ learning within Higher Education. The promises of social media to support learning networks and engage students in more active learning arrangements seem to be an obvious opportunity for university teachers to tap into the rich digital learning ecologies students are already part of. However, while it is well-established that students are heavy users of social media services, such as Facebook, it is equally becoming clear that they are not necessarily well-versed in terms of creating productive learning networks or engaging in web-based activities particularly related to learning or academia (Clark et al. 2009, Luckin et al. 2009). We argue that learning networks based on social media and employed for academic purposes may challenge the traditional norms and practices for both teachers and students within institutionalized learning and therefore need re-negotiation and support.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Ryberg, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-001766"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Active learning","Digital Learning Ecologies","Higher education","Learning","Learning Networks","Networked Learning","Networks","Productive learning","Social media","Web 2 0"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creating a peer driven learning network in higher education using web 000000000002 000000000000 tools to facilitate online dialogue and collaboration","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9780415816564/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-001766","identifier":[{"id":"84917365984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-22f94ab0-374a-4fa5-a3e5-689372d47f49","itu-f43b4c86-3fad-4c29-b156-c0d36085a7c1"],"keyword":["Active Learning","Digital Learning Ecologies","Higher Education","Learning Networks","Networked Learning","Social Media","learning","networks","productive learning","web 2.0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-2-BB4167884A602CFD3D932DBB5109F324"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9780415816564/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, E-learning lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"fc0c09b9-7317-48b6-9bdb-a09739397660","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0003-0355-7421","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"rybergpau","last":"Ryberg","locid":"f05994d0-d004-4702-96d9-1974cfdc2a28","name":"Ryberg, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-1049-8239","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lucila","key":"carvalhopedh","last":"Carvalho","name":"Carvalho, Lucila","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"goodyearpedh","last":"Goodyear","name":"Goodyear, Peter","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780415816557","9780415816564"],"pages":"94-108","publisher":"RoutledgeFalmer","status":"p","title":"The Architecture of Productive Learning Networks"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-22f94ab0-374a-4fa5-a3e5-689372d47f49","itu-f43b4c86-3fad-4c29-b156-c0d36085a7c1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Creating a peer-driven learning network in higher education – using Web 2.0 tools to facilitate online dialogue and collaboration","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-001766","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This article investigates how social software such as blogs can be used to collect ideas generated by the users in the service innovation process. After a theoretical discussion of user involvement and more specifically user involvement using social software and interactive web-tools, the article reports the results from a field experiment at a university library. In the experiment, a blog was established to collect ideas for service innovations from the library users. The experiment shows that blogs may generate a modest, but very useful amount of ideas. The experiment furthermore reveals that blogs might be useful to provide the institution with an image of openness and willingness to listen to customer input.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Scupola, Ada","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-010282"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Interactive Web tools","Library Experiment","Service innovation","Social Software","User involvement"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using social media for service innovations challenges and pitfalls","src":["aau","itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4018/jebr.2013070102","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-010282","identifier":[{"id":"84887419331","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d7175af9-38e4-4918-a19b-2841b1704f96","itu-ffe32245-e808-43cb-9fba-a25871a5f92d","ruc-97075ff6-d991-4176-af18-ab8c41a05a7a"],"keyword":["Interactive Web-tools","Library Experiment","Service Innovation","Social Software","User Involvement"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3DB254528C190484DC32CE1D3090A849"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/48143442/article_IJEBR_9_3_fair_use_policy_version_for_web_site.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4018/jebr.2013070102","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.igi-global.com/article/using-social-media-for-service-innovations/79264","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, The Department of Communication, Business and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Ada","key":"scupolapau","last":"Scupola","locid":"31120161-69fe-4720-8fd6-46383ba639df","name":"Scupola, Ada","orcid":"0000-0002-3537-7639","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"fc0c09b9-7317-48b6-9bdb-a09739397660","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0003-0355-7421","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4018/jebr.2013070102","issn":["15481131","1548114X"],"issn_org":["15481131"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of e-Business Research","pages":"27-37","status":"p","title":"International Journal of e-Business Research","title_org":"International Journal of E-Business Research","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887419331"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d7175af9-38e4-4918-a19b-2841b1704f96","itu-ffe32245-e808-43cb-9fba-a25871a5f92d","ruc-97075ff6-d991-4176-af18-ab8c41a05a7a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Using Social Media for Service Innovations : Challenges and Pitfalls","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-010282","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Background. The ability of pathogens to adapt to the widely used biocide, triclosan, varies substantially. The purpose of the study was to examine bacterial adaptation over an extended period of time to low increments of triclosan concentrations. Focus was two human pathogens, S. aureus and L. monocytogenes that previously have displayed inherent high and low adaptability, respectively. Results. Three strains of L. monocytogenes and two strains of S. aureus including the community-acquired USA300 were exposed to increasing, sub-lethal concentrations of triclosan in triclosan-containing agar gradients. Following 25 days of exposure on agar plates to sub-lethal concentrations of triclosan with a twofold concentration increase every second day, minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) for S. aureus increased from 0.125 (8325-4) and 0.0625 (USA 300) mg/L to 4 mg/L. The MIC of all three L. monocytogenes strains was initially 4 mg/L and remained unaltered by the exposure. The adapted S. aureus isolates retained normal colony size but displayed increased expression of fabI encoding an essential enzyme in bacterial fatty acid synthesis. Also, they displayed decreased or no expression of the virulence associated agrC of the agr quorum sensing system. While most adapted strains of USA300 carried mutations in fabI, none of the adapted strains of 8325-4 did. Conclusions. Adaptability to triclosan varies substantially between Gram positive human pathogens. S. aureus displayed an intrinsically lower MIC for triclosan compared to L. monocytogenes but was easily adapted leading to the same MIC as L. monocytogenes. Even though all adapted S. aureus strains over-expressed fabI and eliminated expression of the agr quorum sensing system, adaptation in USA300 involved fabI mutations whereas this was not the case for 8325-4. Thus, adaptation to triclosan by S. aureus appears to involve multiple genetic pathways.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Larsen, Marianne Halberg","Skovgaard, Sissel","Kastbjerg, Vicky Gaedt","Westh, Henrik","Gram, Lone","Ingmer, Hanne"],"cuid":["S02-082.88-033707"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biocides","Food safety","Gene expression","Listeria","Listeria monocytogenes","Staphylococcus","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Division of Industrial Food Research"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"em staphylococcus aureus em but not em listeria monocytogenes em adapt to triclosan and adaptation correlates with increased em fabi em expression and em agr em deficiency","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/72861303/1471_2180_13_177.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.88-033707","identifier":[{"id":"84880865848","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23898801","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3733935","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-329ae1b0-fb25-4942-b22f-864cd26e3d75","ku-2dc98de5-dce9-4df5-9eac-049729309147"],"keyword":["BIOCIDES","FOOD SAFETY","GENE EXPRESSION","LISTERIA","LISTERIA MONOCYTOGENES","STAPHYLOCOCCUS","STAPHYLOCOCCUS AUREUS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C84C5257D925E33075EF0B1F474F9AC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/72861303/1471_2180_13_177.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2180-13-177","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Food Safety and Zoonoses"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Division of Industrial Food Research"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1a4f890a-d171-4c2f-ae00-dd1e024c25ab","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne Halberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"da445e7f-59a6-4e1c-ad17-57e0e317ce6a","name":"Larsen, Marianne Halberg","orcid":"0000-0001-6242-6937","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sissel","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Sissel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vicky Gaedt","key":"kastbjergpau","last":"Kastbjerg","locid":"30893771-6d05-44ad-bc8f-7fb706310d52","name":"Kastbjerg, Vicky Gaedt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Henrik T.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, Henrik T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone","key":"grampau","last":"Gram","locid":"9fabd1ae-e28f-4a5d-8456-7a075b4aa34e","name":"Gram, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-1076-5723","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23898801"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2180-13-177","issn":["14712180"],"issue":"177","journal":"BMC Microbiology","paperid":"177","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"BMC Microbiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880865848"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-329ae1b0-fb25-4942-b22f-864cd26e3d75","ku-2dc98de5-dce9-4df5-9eac-049729309147"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Staphylococcus aureus but not Listeria monocytogenes adapt to triclosan and adaptation correlates with increased fabI expression and agr deficiency.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.88-033707","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The increasing use of mobile phones and services introduces the challenging questionof how to take advantage of the services without the service providers taking advantage of us. The notion of location-based services often means a less transparent partner and may constitute a challenge too big for some users to be a part of the natural developments in mobile services. This paper focuses on one segment of Danish mobile phone users who are trailing behind advanced mobile users but have an interest in trends and technological developments. The overall purpose is to gain an insight into this segment’s perception of location - based services by focusing on different existing and forthcoming services. The paper concludes that users are generally willing to disclose location-based data if they find the services useful and to their advantage. Privacy and trust are essential elements in judging this perspective.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bjørner, Thomas","Sørensen, Lene Tolstrup","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120395"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Location based services","Qualitative interview"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it s pretty smart but also a bit frightening a qualitative study about mobile tracking among danish mobile users","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/82479894/cmi_working_paper_3.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-120395","ids":["aau-f1f157f8-a32c-44fd-b0fc-daf4aa9a9bb3"],"keyword":["Buzz users","Location based services","Qualitative interview","mobile tracking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9BEDD2AB7527C65F9CB9D8040A866FBA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/82479894/cmi_working_paper_3.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.cmi.aau.dk/digitalAssets/77/77578_a-qualitative-study-about-mobile-tracking-among-danish-mobile-users_cmi_wp3.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Mobility and Tracking Technologies","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Augmented Cognition Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"bjørnerpau","last":"Bjørner","locid":"65c6cc27-0e30-49d1-aa84-7cbc986fa9e1","name":"Bjørner, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-9071-7168","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Tolstrup","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4b286010-6708-428f-9a5f-ada197a8f02f","name":"Sørensen, Lene Tolstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2573-0750","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"fc0c09b9-7317-48b6-9bdb-a09739397660","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0003-0355-7421","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"3","pages":"26","place":"København","publisher":"Center for Communication, Media and Information technologies (CMI), Electronic Systems, Aalborg University Copenhagen","repno":"CMI Working Paper, No. 3","series":"CMI Working Paper","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f1f157f8-a32c-44fd-b0fc-daf4aa9a9bb3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"It's pretty smart but also a bit frightening : A qualitative study about mobile tracking among Danish mobile users","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-120395","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Chlorhexidine is used as a disinfectant to prevent surgical infections. Recently, studies have indicated that chlorhexidine usage has selected methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus strains that are tolerant to chlorhexidine and that this may be related to the presence of the qacA/B-encoded efflux pumps. Here, we evaluated if high-level exposure to chlorhexidine selects for tolerant colonizing Staphylococcus epidermidis and we addressed the consequences of long-term exposure to chlorhexidine.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Skovgaard, Sissel","Larsen, Marianne Halberg","Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Skov, Robert Leo","Wong, Christian","Westh, Henrik","Ingmer, Hanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505246"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recently introduced em qaca b em genes in em staphylococcus epidermidis em do not increase chlorhexidine mic mbc","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jac/dkt182","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-505246","identifier":[{"id":"23739538","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84887822370","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bb510e1b-0ee1-4e27-be4e-10876daf2635"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5A21D61D0F7D71915CC3EF5FF2B66A26"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/jac/dkt182","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Food Safety and Zoonoses"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sissel","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Sissel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marianne Halberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"da445e7f-59a6-4e1c-ad17-57e0e317ce6a","name":"Larsen, Marianne Halberg","orcid":"0000-0001-6242-6937","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1a4f890a-d171-4c2f-ae00-dd1e024c25ab","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Robert Leo","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Robert Leo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik T.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, Henrik T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23739538"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/jac/dkt182","issn":["03057453","14602091"],"issn_org":["03057453"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Antimicrobial Chemotherapy","pages":"2226-2233","status":"p","title":"Journal of Antimicrobial Chemotherapy","title_org":"The Journal of antimicrobial chemotherapy","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887822370"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bb510e1b-0ee1-4e27-be4e-10876daf2635"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Recently introduced <em>qacA/B</em> genes in <em>Staphylococcus epidermidis</em> do not increase chlorhexidine MIC/MBC","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505246","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Since its introduction to the market in the 1970s, the synthetic biocide triclosan has had widespread use in household and medical products. Although decreased triclosan susceptibility has been observed for several bacterial species, when exposed under laboratory settings, no in vivo studies have associated triclosan use with decreased triclosan susceptibility or cross-resistance to antibiotics. One major challenge of such studies is the lack of strains that with certainty have not been exposed to triclosan. Here we have overcome this challenge by comparing current isolates of the human opportunistic pathogen Staphylococcus epidermidis with isolates collected in the 1960s prior to introduction of triclosan to the market. Of 64 current S. epidermidis isolates 12.5% were found to have tolerance towards triclosan defined as MIC≥0.25 mg/l compared to none of 34 isolates obtained in the 1960s. When passaged in the laboratory in the presence of triclosan, old and current susceptible isolates could be adapted to the same triclosan MIC level as found in current tolerant isolates. DNA sequence analysis revealed that laboratory-adapted strains carried mutations in fabI encoding the enoyl-acyl carrier protein reductase isoform, FabI, that is the target of triclosan, and the expression of fabI was also increased. However, the majority of the tolerant current isolates carried no mutations in fabI or the putative promoter region. Thus, this study indicates that the widespread use of triclosan has resulted in the occurrence of S. epidermidis with tolerance towards triclosan and that the adaptation involves FabI as well as other factors. We suggest increased caution in the general application of triclosan as triclosan has not shown efficacy in reducing infections and is toxic to aquatic organisms.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Skovgaard, Sissel","Nielsen, Lene Nørby","Larsen, Marianne Halberg","Skov, Robert Leo","Ingmer, Hanne","Westh, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416204"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anti Infective Agents Local","Drug Resistance Bacterial","Microbial Sensitivity Tests","Staphylococcus epidermidis","Time Factors","Triclosan"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"em staphylococcus epidermidis em isolated in 000000001965 are more susceptible to triclosan than current isolates","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0062197","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416204","identifier":[{"id":"84876182475","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23614034","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3628582","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-261cc82e-bc64-45db-8418-a270ed5d22a5"],"keyword":["Anti-Infective Agents, Local","Drug Resistance, Bacterial","Microbial Sensitivity Tests","Staphylococcus epidermidis","Time Factors","Triclosan"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D9D41DD243BB076A85807D59260B90B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0062197","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Food Safety and Zoonoses"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sissel","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","name":"Skovgaard, Sissel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Nørby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1a4f890a-d171-4c2f-ae00-dd1e024c25ab","name":"Nielsen, Lene Nørby","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marianne Halberg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"da445e7f-59a6-4e1c-ad17-57e0e317ce6a","name":"Larsen, Marianne Halberg","orcid":"0000-0001-6242-6937","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Robert Leo","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Robert Leo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik T.","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"5ed71556-672c-4f57-95de-3abba6b821ea","name":"Westh, Henrik","name_org":"Westh, Henrik T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23614034"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0062197","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e62197","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84876182475"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All