{"abstract":"This article investigates the use of social software such as blogs to communicate with and to involve users in the idea generation process of service innovations. After a theoretical discussion of user involvement and more specifically user involvement using web-tools with specific focus on blogs, the article reports findings and lessons from a field experiment at a university library. In the experiment, a blog was established to collect service innovation ideas from the library users. The experiment shows that a blog may engage a limited number of users in the idea generation process and generate a useful, but modest amount of ideas.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Scupola, Ada","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S02-093.95-004007"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"library perceptions of using social software as blogs in the idea generation phase of service innovations lessons from an experiment","src":["aau","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-37228-5_14","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.95-004007","identifier":[{"id":"84983039628","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-52145b6c-c5ed-4cdb-9514-de27120a14d2","ruc-a9168dd7-bbf3-459d-9723-c4aa25818747"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3D813186BA4B2B1A8818A6612533CF05"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-37228-5_14","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde Universit