{"abstract":"The use of Web 2.0 in higher education to enrich learning through active student participation is promising however not straightforward. This paper reports on the challenges derived from the students' reflected experiences on using ediscussions in a course as a supplement to traditional teaching methods such as lectures and traditional types of group work. The insight generated point towards a number of considerations when integration e-discussion as part of a course, especially the lack of qualifications using Web 2.0 technologies for learning, transparency of student resources, changed roles and growing stress are challenges of importance.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-055576"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-23","place":"Rome, it","start":"2011-07-20","title":"IADIS International Conference e-Learning 2011, Part of the IADIS Multi Conference on Computer Science and Information Systems 2011, MCCSIS 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"keyword":["Empirical study","Higher education","Learning design","Social learning","Web 2 0"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for social learning in higher education using web 000000000002 000000000000","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84865068662&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-055576","identifier":[{"id":"84865068662","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-12fdde57-1899-45b2-8b02-a470532e5d22"],"keyword":["Empirical study","Higher education","Learning design","Social learning","Web 2.0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1660BFAB9BA9284B41E774A50E65FC08"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"fc0c09b9-7317-48b6-9bdb-a09739397660","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0003-0355-7421","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789728939380"],"pages":"246-250","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IADIS International Conference e-Learning 2011, Part of the IADIS Multi Conference on Computer Science and Information Systems 2011, MCCSIS 2011","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865068662"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-12fdde57-1899-45b2-8b02-a470532e5d22"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Designing for social learning in higher education using Web 2.0","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055576","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Purpose - The paper investigates how customers may contribute to radical innovation in consultancy services and what are the conditions needed for customers to involve in such radical service innovations. Design/methodology/approach - The paper uses a qualitative case study approach including rich descriptions based primarily on interviews to investigate an extreme example of successful customer involvement in the development of radical service innovations in Ramboll, a leading Scandinavian engineering consultancy. Findings – Our study reveals that customers may be involved in radical innovation processes to different degrees. However involving customers actively in radical services innovation require a relationship between the customer company and the service provider that might be described as a partnership in which ongoing learning is taking place to develop new solutions. Our findings reveal that unsolved problems as well as personal trust are keys in order to make customers involve in radical service innovations. Customers involved actively are further characterized by possessing high expertise and extraordinary personal engagement. Research limitations/implications – As in all case studies, the main limitation of our study is the generalizability of the findings. More cases would help to shed light on the generalizability of the findings across other radical innovation projects within the same company or in similar type of companies. Originality/value – The study contributes with new and detailed insights into both how to involve customers in radical service innovations and the conditions and challenges found in doing so. Paper type: Research Paper","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Hugger, Ada Scupola"],"cuid":["S03-094.48-004935"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Case studies","Case study","Customer involvement","Customer services quality","Engineering consulting","Quality Improvement","Radical innovation","Scandinavia","Service innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating issues and challenges for customer involvement in business services innovation","src":["aau","itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/33011379/Journal_of_Business_and_Industrial_marketing_Vo._26_5_Ramb_ll.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-094.48-004935","identifier":[{"id":"79958764139","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000295191700007","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-65cfdeed-eb33-4db4-9f4c-ffb29df4e6b0","itu-3afceb8f-66e9-423e-a070-e3a17ddc53b5","ruc-34ec1c4e-75f9-40b7-9bb2-44aed0528dd8"],"keyword":["Case studies","Case study","Customer involvement","Customer services quality","Engineering consulting","Quality improvement,","Radical innovation","Scandinavia","Scandinaviact","Service innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B049355957251A57C1EE5510116D24FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1108/08858621111144424","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.emeraldinsight.com/journals.htm?articleid=1927490&show=abstract","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/33011379/Journal_of_Business_and_Industrial_marketing_Vo._26_5_Ramb_ll.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Euro